{"file": "D:\\SpaceBook\\_cls7_jpg\\eng\\088.jpg", "lines": [{"text": "Floods are caused or amplified by both natural and man", "conf": 0.946, "box": [[267, 292], [1173, 198], [1178, 248], [272, 342]]}, {"text": "made factors. Major weather factors include heavy or", "conf": 0.922, "box": [[267, 344], [1172, 253], [1176, 299], [272, 390]]}, {"text": "prolonged precipitation, snow melt, thunderstorms, storm", "conf": 0.947, "box": [[269, 396], [1172, 304], [1176, 350], [274, 442]]}, {"text": "surges from hurricanes, and ice or debris jams. Human", "conf": 0.929, "box": [[268, 448], [1170, 357], [1174, 400], [272, 491]]}, {"text": "factors include structural failures of dams and levees, altered", "conf": 0.945, "box": [[268, 495], [1168, 407], [1172, 453], [272, 541]]}, {"text": "drainage, and land cover alterations (such as pavement).", "conf": 0.909, "box": [[267, 544], [1090, 469], [1094, 515], [271, 590]]}, {"text": "Heat Waves", "conf": 0.81, "box": [[271, 635], [462, 623], [464, 657], [273, 669]]}, {"text": "Heat waves are periods of abnormally hot weather lasting", "conf": 0.921, "box": [[265, 683], [1179, 604], [1183, 652], [269, 731]]}, {"text": "days to weeks. The number of heat waves has been increasing", "conf": 0.942, "box": [[268, 734], [1178, 658], [1181, 702], [272, 777]]}, {"text": "in recent years. This trend has continued over the years, with", "conf": 0.929, "box": [[265, 783], [1179, 707], [1182, 754], [269, 829]]}, {"text": "the number of intense heat waves being trippled. The recent", "conf": 0.922, "box": [[266, 832], [1181, 761], [1185, 808], [270, 879]]}, {"text": "heat waves and droughts in many countries have set records", "conf": 0.949, "box": [[264, 882], [1180, 811], [1184, 861], [268, 932]]}, {"text": "for the highest monthly average temperatures. Analyses show", "conf": 0.91, "box": [[266, 932], [1178, 865], [1182, 914], [270, 981]]}, {"text": "that human-induced climate change has generally increased", "conf": 0.923, "box": [[265, 982], [1178, 917], [1181, 965], [269, 1030]]}, {"text": "the probability of heat waves.", "conf": 0.881, "box": [[269, 1036], [698, 1014], [700, 1051], [271, 1073]]}, {"text": "Drought", "conf": 0.873, "box": [[269, 1102], [414, 1097], [415, 1143], [271, 1148]]}, {"text": "Higher temperatures lead to increased rates of evaporation,", "conf": 0.89, "box": [[271, 1156], [1180, 1102], [1183, 1144], [273, 1199]]}, {"text": "including more loss of moisture through plant leaves. As soil", "conf": 0.949, "box": [[269, 1205], [1183, 1151], [1186, 1197], [271, 1251]]}, {"text": "dries out, a larger proportion of the incoming heat from the", "conf": 0.925, "box": [[271, 1257], [1182, 1205], [1185, 1248], [273, 1300]]}, {"text": "sun absorbs heating the soil and adjacent air rather than", "conf": 0.917, "box": [[272, 1310], [1181, 1261], [1183, 1299], [274, 1348]]}, {"text": "evaporating its moisture, resulting in hotter summers under", "conf": 0.941, "box": [[273, 1362], [1178, 1314], [1180, 1352], [275, 1399]]}, {"text": "drierclimaticconditions", "conf": 0.925, "box": [[274, 1408], [626, 1397], [627, 1430], [275, 1442]]}, {"text": "Vocabulary", "conf": 0.819, "box": [[337, 1500], [595, 1505], [594, 1553], [337, 1548]]}, {"text": "Read the meanings of the given words.", "conf": 0.911, "box": [[317, 1589], [927, 1568], [929, 1605], [319, 1626]]}, {"text": "clouds, strong wind, rain, hail", "conf": 0.921, "box": [[805, 1630], [1252, 1616], [1253, 1655], [806, 1669]]}, {"text": "tornado", "conf": 0.851, "box": [[412, 1644], [537, 1642], [537, 1680], [412, 1682]]}, {"text": "hurricaneorcyclone", "conf": 0.886, "box": [[412, 1701], [712, 1696], [713, 1733], [412, 1738]]}, {"text": "strong wind, heavy rain", "conf": 0.903, "box": [[803, 1693], [1157, 1684], [1158, 1720], [804, 1729]]}, {"text": "blizzard", "conf": 0.824, "box": [[412, 1759], [535, 1759], [535, 1800], [412, 1800]]}, {"text": "heavy snow, ice, cold temperatures", "conf": 0.944, "box": [[801, 1753], [1345, 1744], [1345,